</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>44412-03-00</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>52.64 max &plusmn;3%</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>23.88 max &plusmn;3%</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="870" seq="804"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-870-804-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Dimensions</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>For dimensions <grphcref
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-015-A01"></grphcref>.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="015" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-015-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Dimensions</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-015-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="ap"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-015-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-015-A01-02" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-015-A01-02" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-015-A01-03" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-015-A01-03" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="870" seq="805"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-870-805-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Equipment Identification Plate</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>For equipment identification plate <refint
reftype="Figure" refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-016-A01"></refint></para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Identification plate part number 00-5008 to be stuck
on the back of the bottom foam. The TSO or QAC approval does not cover
any electronic equipment such as or its installation (if applicable).
The installer of the seat into the aircraft must substantiate these
additional components.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>It is necessary to communicate the equipment (seat/shell/monument/console)
P/N and S/N when ordering new identification placards. They are supplied
with all necessary information already printed.</para>
</note>
<note><para>Use self adhesive transparent plastic film P/N AE404 (ALT
P/N PDFILMPP100X65) to prevent damage to the surface of the identification
plate P/N 00-5008 (ALT P/N F0554720).</para>
</note>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="016" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-016-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Equipment
Identification Plate</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-016-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-016-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="870" seq="806"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0001" chg="u"
key="Task-25-15-65-870-806-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Modification placards</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Equipment Modification Placard</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>For equipment modification placard <grphcref
refid="Graphic-25-15-65-991-017-A01"></grphcref>.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>The equipment modification placard P/N 00-6414 (ALT P/N
F0554722) must be installed near the existing Equipment identification
placard.</para>
</note>
<note><para>Use self-adhesive transparent plastic film P/N AE404 (ALT
P/N PDFILMPP100X65) to prevent damage to the surface of the equipment
modification placard P/N 00-6414 (ALT P/N F0554722).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Add or complete the equipment modification
placard P/N 00-6414 (ALT P/N F0554722) on each modified equipment
to indicate that a Service Bulletin and its revision has been completed.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="017"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0001" confnbr="1" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-017-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Modification
Placard</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-017-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-017-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Component modification placard</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>For component modification placard <grphcref
refid="Graphic-25-15-65-991-018-A01"></grphcref>.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>The component modification placard P/N F0523885 (ALT P/N
F0555661) must be installed near the existing Component identification
placard.</para>
</note>
<note><para>Use self-adhesive transparent plastic film P/N AE404 (ALT
P/N PDFILMPP100X65) to prevent damage to the surface of the component
modification placard P/N F0523885 (ALT P/N F0555661).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Add or complete the equipment modification
placard P/N 00-6414 (ALT P/N F0554722) on each modified equipment
to indicate that a Service Bulletin and its revision has been completed.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="018"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0001" confnbr="1" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-018-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Modification
placard</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-018-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-018-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>In the case when a seat has the previous identification
placard P/N 00-5008 or modification placard P/N 00-6414 or 00-7371
containing a legible seat&rsquo;s information, it is not mandatory
to replace them.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>When an SB kit is ordered and containing the previous
identification placard P/N 00-5008 or modification placard P/N 00-6414
or 00-7371, the new identification placard P/N F0554720 or modification
placard P/N F0554722 or F0554723 will be received instead.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>This SIL can be used as an interchangeability document
regarding the identification and modification placards.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="1001" chg="u"
key="PGBLK-25-15-65-1001-" revdate="20250131">
<title>TESTING AND FAULT ISOLATION</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="700" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-700-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Testing</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Reason for the job</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>This chapter provides the procedures to make sure that
the equipment is in good condition, controlling the condition and
the characteristics of the equipment.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tools, features and equipment</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Consumables</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Referenced information</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="101"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-101-A01">
<tgroup cols="2"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.26*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="0.74*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Reference</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Designation</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-300-801-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Repair</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-870-801-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Description and operation</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Test conditions</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Ambient temperature: 15 &deg;C to 30 &deg;C (59 &deg;F to 86
&deg;F).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Ambient atmospheric pressure.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Relative humidity: &le;&nbsp;90%.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The various incidents that may be encountered are listed below
along with their probable causes.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Repair defective parts, <refint reftype="1"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-6001-">(refer to Page Block 6001) "REPAIR"</refint> by
approved workshops or replace with serviceable elements. Make sure
that you use only approved parts you can invalidate the certification.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Procedure</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Seat testing</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>The tests consist in putting the seat in its serviceable position
and the examination of the good working order of all its different
components.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine the correct lowering movement of the seating assembly,
make sure it manually goes back and the door moves correctly, and
that there are no friction points and that it operates without any
problems.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Dimensional inspection.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine that the overall dimensions of the seat are compliant
with dimensions paragraph <refint reftype="TASK"
refid="Task-25-15-65-870-804-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Functional tests.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<title>Longitudinal adjustment</title>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the unlocking</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>When the lever is pushed down, the studs must
simultaneously get out of the indexing holes without hard point.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the sliding of the seat track (without rear fairing)</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The seat must slide without noise and the stud
must not contact the track.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the locking on the track</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Lock the seat by releasing the handle.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Studs must fit into the holes at the same time
without bending.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the emergency unlocking system (3 levers)</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Unload the seat, the above five tests to be
done to make sure the system works without any problem <refint
reftype="0" refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-101-A01"></refint>.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Height adjustment</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the up and down adjustment using the electrical actuator.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Push the upper part of the switch. The seat
must go up without hard points and stop at the end stop.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Push the lower part of the switch. The seat
must go down without hard points and stop at the end stop.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the functioning of the mechanical back-up adjustment
in height.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>No hard points.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Lateral adjustment</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the unlocking.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The seat is in the maxi rear position, the
handle is released upwards, the seat must be released for the next
slide.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the manual unlock system.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Sliding without noise and without a hard point.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the locking.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The handle is released and the seat does not
move any more.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Backrest</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the backrest recline.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>No interference between the fairings during
the reclining position, up to the maximum reclining position.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the locking.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The backrest must stay in the defined position.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the unlocking.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The backrest must return to the upright position
(without constraint).</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Pull the lateral lever to activate the recline actuator.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Make sure that the lever does not have too
much play and that it returns to its initial position when released.</para>
<para></para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Push the lateral lever to activate the recline cylinder. The
lever must not have too much gap and must return to its initial position
when released.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="101"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-101-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Emergency
Unlocking System (3 Levers)</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-101-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-101-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Restraint system.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that every component of the harness is correctly attached
with the buckle.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Each element must lock on the buckle.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that no belt is caught when the buckle is activated.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>No element must get caught.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the two mounting screws on the pelvis straps
(1 per side) are correctly tightened.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Fastener must be able to pivot.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that shoulder belts can wind up correctly to the stop
(strap guide), and at a consistent speed.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The necessary time for the rolling-up of the
belts between maximum deployment and propped up over guides must be
between 1 and 2 seconds.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that pelvis straps adjusters are working correctly.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Deploy and fold-up the pelvis straps via the
adjuster (up to abutment on each side).</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the locking mechanism of the inertia reel is
working correctly.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Pull sharply on the shoulder belts and the
inertia reel must be blocked.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Procedure to remind headrest structure usage for good practices</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>Do NOT rotate the headrest.</para>
</caution>
<para>The headrest assembly move up and down and the headrest have
a angular movement of &plusmn;15&ordm;. In any case don't use the
headrest as handle.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="810" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-810-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Fault Isolation Procedures</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>The possible failures causes for this equipment could
be due to a defective assembly or adjustment during the assembly of
various sub-assemblies.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>An incorrect use could be a source of incidents. In
all these cases, remove and replace the defective parts.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>Structural or attaching hardware is not covered in the
trouble shooting procedure. These items have no operational characteristics
to examine, a visual inspection for looseness, broken, cracked or
damaged parts will indicate the cause of the trouble and the corrective
action to be taken. <refint reftype="0"
refid="table-25-15-65-992-102-a01"></refint> to locate faults in the
seat assembly applicable to a subassembly or to an individual part.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>Once the indicated repairs performed, try out the seat
again to ensure that the fault no longer exists, <refint reftype="1"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-0001-">(refer to Page Block 0001) "DESCRIPTION
AND OPERATION"</refint>.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>The most frequently encountered failures during use
of the equipment are listed in the table below, as well as the possible
causes and corresponding repairs to be performed.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="102"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1001" frame="all"
id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-102-A01">
<title>Fault Isolation Procedures</title>
<tgroup cols="3"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="0.97*"><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.03*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry namest="col1" nameend="col3" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>Fault Isolation Procedures</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Trouble</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Probable Cause</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Corrective Action</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="3">
<para>The seat has seized up, in the up and down position.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>The electrical actuator is defective.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine the electrical actuator  and replace if necessary.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>The electrical actuator attaching screws have seized up or are defective.
</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine the electrical actuator attaching screws and replace if necessary.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>The switch is defective.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine the switch and replace the harness if necessary.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Electrical harness cut or wrongly connected.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine for correct connection. Replace defective harness if necessary.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" rowsep="1">
<para>Restraint System Reel does not operate  correctly.</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Inertia reel malfunctioning.</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="1">
<para>Examine shape good winding.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Replace the inertia reel.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Backrest has seized up.</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="1">
<para>Defective backrest hydrolocks.</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="1">
<para>Replace the backrest hydrolock.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Seized up or damaged mechanical control mechanism.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace the control mechanism.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" rowsep="1">
<para>Angular adjustment is impossible for armrest.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Button improperly adjusted.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Tighten or loosen the front knob.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Wheel improperly adjusted.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Tighten or loosen screws.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Seat tilt handle is broken away.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Vibrations, shocks.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace or adjust the tilt handle.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="2">
<para>Longitudinal/Lateral adjustment is impossible.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Broken control cable.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace control cable.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Dust, object...</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine the lateral aft and front crosspiece.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Remove dust or foreign object from the track. Examine the lateral rear and front crosspiece.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="3">
<para>Longitudinal/Lateral adjustment is difficult.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Bearing worn.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace bearing.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Friction of the pin on the track.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Adjust cables.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Dust, object...</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine the lateral aft and front crosspiece.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Remove dust or foreign object from the track. Examine the lateral rear and front crosspiece.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" rowsep="1">
<para>Vertical adjustment is difficult or impossible.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Presence of foreign objects.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Remove any foreign objects.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Electrical system.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine actuator and wiring.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Thighrest adjustment is difficult.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Defective thighrest hydrolock.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace the thighrest hydrolock.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Seized up or damaged mechanical control mechanism.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace the control mechanism.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Armrest loose / will not stay in position</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>The armrest screw is removed.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace armrest screw.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Noisy actuator</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Defective actuator, actuator ball bearing or reduction gear.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace electrical actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Actuator does not rotate</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Open-circuit warning harness.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace wiring harness.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Open-circuit actuator wires or worn actuator brushes or broken gear.
</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace electrical actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Inoperative manual override</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Broken actuator/gearbox.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace electrical actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Deformed hexagonal override shaft.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace electrical actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>In manual or electrical operation, actuator rotates but the shaft does not move
</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Defective slip clutch.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace electrical actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Actuator shut down when at a  mechanical limit.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Defective slip clutch.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace electrical actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem><?Pub _newline>
