</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Procedure</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-001-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Upholstery Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-950-802-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the bottom cushion assy <csn refid="id-2-190"></csn> composed
of bottom foam <csn refid="id-2-200"></csn> and bottom cover <csn
refid="id-2-210"></csn>, the backrest cushion  assy <csn
refid="id-2-220"></csn> composed of backrest foam <csn refid="id-2-230"></csn> and
backrest cover <csn refid="id-2-240"></csn>, and the headrest foams <csn
refid="id-2-290"></csn>, <csn refid="id-2-295"></csn>, <csn
refid="id-2-300"></csn> and the headrest cover <csn refid="id-2-305"></csn> from
their supports.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Fairing Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-345-A01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-003-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove four screws (20) then remove backrest fairing (10).</para>
<note><para>To remove backrest fairing (10) you can tilt the backrest.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove four screws (40) then remove upper link fairing (30).</para>
<note><para>To remove upper link fairing (30) you can put the seat
in upper position and the backrest in upright position.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove six screws (60) then remove aft fairing (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove four screws (80) then remove bottom outboard fairing
(70).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove five screws (100) then remove bottom inboard fairing
(90).</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="345" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-345-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Fairing
Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-345-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-345-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-003-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Headrest Assembly Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-346-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Loosen two screws (190).</para>
<note><para>It is not necessary to fully loosen the screws to remove
the headrest.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove headrest by pulling it upward from backrest structure.</para><?Pub
_newline>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="346" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-346-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Headrest
Assembly Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-346-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-346-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-004-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Restraint System Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-347-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-003-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove aft nut (40), washers (30) and screw (20) then disengage
the inertia reel (10) from backrest structure.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Unclip lateral belts (10) from seat belt attach (150).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove nut (90), washers (70), spacer (60) and screw (50) of
the attachment fitting of the front safety belt to the seat pan structure.
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove nuts (120), screws (100), untie sandow and remove mechanical
command (10).</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="347" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-347-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Restraint
System Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-347-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-347-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-005-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Electrical Actuator Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-950-801-A01"> </grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-348-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<title>Put seat on full low position.</title>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-003-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para><revst>Remove the aft fairing, <revend><refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Disconnect the electrical connector from the electrical actuator
(500).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>IF THE actuator DOES NOT OPERATE, USE THE CRANK TO
PUT THE SEAT IN UP OR DOWN POSITION <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-950-801-A01"> (Refer to IPL FIG. 1)</refint>.</para>
</caution>
<para>Loosen nut (515) of upper shaft (505) of electrical actuator
(500). Remove spacers (510). Remove upper shaft (505).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Push lower shaft (545) to bring it out from lower links (455)
and (460). Remove electrical actuator (500).</para>
<?Pub _newline>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="348" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-348-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Actuator
Assembly Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-348-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-348-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-006-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Tilt Hydrolock and Control Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-349-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-003-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the rod fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>do NOT loose screws (140).</para>
</caution>
<para>Loosen screws (140) then disconnect hydrolock head control (130).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove shaft (210).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove screw (230), remove washer (240) and nut (250).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove hydrolock (200).</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="349" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-349-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Tilt
Hydrolock and Control Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-349-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-349-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-007-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Backrest from Seat Pan Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-350-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="subtask-25-15-65-040-003-a01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the seat pan fairings, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Disconnect the hydrolock head control, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-006-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove mechanical command of restraint system <refint
reftype="SUBTASK" refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-004-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>BEFORE YOU REMOVE THE CABLE, MARK THE ROUTING OF THE
CABLE AND THE POSITION OF CABLE CLAMPS WITH A SOFT LEAD PENCIL.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove all cables interfering between backrest and seat pan<refint
reftype="SUBTASK" refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-011-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove shafts (140), remove washers (150) and nuts (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Push downward backrest (130) and remove it.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="350" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-350-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Backrest
from Seat Pan Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-350-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-350-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-008-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Armrest Assembly Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-351-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<title>Unclip armcap (70).</title>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove nut (120), spacers (110), washers (100) and screw (90)
then remove armrest equipped.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="351" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-351-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Armrest
Assembly Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-351-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-351-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-009-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Seat Pan Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-352-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-003-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the seat pan fairings, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Disconnect the hydrolocks, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-006-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>BEFORE YOU REMOVE THE CABLE, MARK THE ROUTING OF THE
CABLE AND THE POSITION OF CABLE CLAMPS WITH A SOFT LEAD PENCIL.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove all cables interfering in the seat pan <refint
reftype="SUBTASK" refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-011-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put seat in upward position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove shafts (30), washers (40), washers (45), spacers (60)
and nuts (50). </para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove seat pan from lower structure.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="352" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-352-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Seat
Pan Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-352-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-352-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-010-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Roller From The Crosspiece Front Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-353-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>REPLACE THE ROLLERS ONE AT A TIME, WITH THE SEAT INSTALLED
ON THE SEAT TRACK, TO MAKE SURE THAT THE ADJUSTMENT OF THE ROLLER
ADJUSTING STOP REMAINS UNCHANGED.</para>
</caution>
<para>Put the seat in upward position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove four screws (30) of front crosspiece (10) and remove
them.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove four rollers (20).</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="353" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-353-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Roller
from the Crosspiece Front Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-353-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-353-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="040" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-011-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Cables Removal</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-354-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove fairings impacted by each removal <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-040-002-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>BEFORE YOU REMOVE THE CABLE, MARK THE ROUTING OF THE
CABLE AND THE POSITION OF CABLE CLAMPS WITH A SOFT LEAD PENCIL.</para>
</caution>
<para>Remove the lateral front control cables (20) and (30A) as follow:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Mark the routing of the lateral front control cables (20) and
(30A) then mark the position of cable clamps with a soft lead pencil.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cut and remove the cable clamps that attach the cable to the
seat pan.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the cable stop (210) and the cotter pin (220) from the
handle (290) and discard it.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the two screws (105) from the cap (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the control pin (100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Lift the assembly (40), (80) and (90) to disengage it.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the circlips (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the lower of the lateral front control cables (20) and
(30A) attached with the cap (80) and with the spring (90).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the lateral front control cable (20) and (30A).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the tilt control cable (50) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Mark the routing of the tilt control cable (90) and the divider
(100) then the position of cable clamps with a soft lead pencil.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cut and remove the cable clamps that attach the cable to the
backrest structure.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the cable stop (210) and the cotter pin (220) from the
handle (290) and discard them.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Loosen the screw (140) from the hydrolocks (200) with an allen
key.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Pull out the tilt control cable (90) from the hydrolocks.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Loosen the upper of the tilt control cable (50) from the holding
bracket (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the tilt control cable (50) attached with the divider
(100).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the longitudinal LH and RH control cable (10) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Mark the routing of the longitudinal LH and RH control cable
(10) and the position of cable clamps with a soft lead pencil.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cut and remove cable clamps that attach cable to seat pan.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove cable stop (210) and cotter pin (220) from handle (290)
and discard them.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove two screws (255) from cap (240).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove front control pin (250).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Lift the assembly (40), (240) and (245) to disengage it.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove circlips (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the lower of the longitudinal LH and RH control cable
(10) attached with cap (240) and spring (245).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove the longitudinal LH and RH control cable (10).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove control handle spring (330) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove screw (370) and washer (360) located at handle (290).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove screw (370) and washer (360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove washer (380) and spring (330).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="354"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-354-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Cables
Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-354-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-354-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-354-A01-02" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-354-A01-02" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="PGBLK-25-15-65-4001-" revdate="20250131">
<title>CLEANING</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="100" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-100-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Cleaning</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Reason for the job</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thorough cleaning is essential to any close
inspection to determine the presence, extent and location of possible
defects. External surfaces and upholstery must be periodically examined
and cleaned.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>ALL THE CLEANING MATERIAL USED MUST BE VALIDATED BY
SAFRAN SEATS FRANCE. IF THE CLEANING MATERIAL IS NOT VALIDATED BY
SAFRAN SEATS FRANCE, THE PARTS WILL DECREASE THE GUARANTEE.</para>
</warning>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up information</title>
<note><para>The table below lists cleaning agents and materials for
use on the seat assembly.</para>
</note>
<note><para>You can use equivalent alternatives for items in the lists.</para>
</note>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tools, features and equipment<?Pub _newline></para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="401"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-401-A01">
<tgroup cols="3"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.00*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Reference</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Qty</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Designation</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>1</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Standard mechanics technician's tool</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Washing machine</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>1</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Vacuum cleaner</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>1</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Cloth</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>1</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Low pressure jet of dehydrated air</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Consumables<?Pub _newline></para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>ALL THE CONSUMABLES SUPPLIED BY SAFRAN AND LISTED INTO
THE CMM CAN HAVE A LIMITED LIFETIME. PLEASE REVIEW LABELS ON CONTAINER
OR EXAMINE THE TECHNICAL DATA SHEET BEFORE USE OR STORE.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DRY THE SEAT AFTER ANY CLEANING.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DURING THE CLEANING, USE CELLOPHANE TO PREVENT DAMAGE
ON THE MATERIAL AS ACTUATOR, HARNESS, SWITCH AND RECLINE LOCK.</para>
</caution>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="402"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-402-A01">
<tgroup cols="3"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.00*">
<thead>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.34in">
<entry namest="col1" nameend="col3" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>Consumables</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.34in">
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Use</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Qty</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Designation</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Metal, dirt and grime</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Soap and water (Ivory liquid soap), chlorinated dry cleaning solvent.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Metal, grease and oil</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Hexane, isopropyl alcohol, grain alcohol (ethanol). Chlorinated dry cleaning solvent.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Fabric backed vinyls</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Soap and water (Ivory liquid soap).</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Polycarbonate/ABS fairing dirt and grime</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Soap and water only.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Leather</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry><revst>
<para>Water-based, pH-neutral soap.</para>
<revend></entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Sheepskin</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Soaps such as Ivory liquid containing no enzymes and a neutral pH. Do not use Woolite.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Pre-washing</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Perchlorethylene.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Washing</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Alcohol.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Referenced information</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<?Pub _newpage>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Procedure</title>
<warning><para>USE CLEANING AGENTS ONLY IN AN AREA WITH A GOOD SUPPLY
OF AIR. OBEY LOCAL SAFETY AND HEALTH INSTRUCTIONS. OBEY THE MANUFACTURERS
INSTRUCTIONS. PUT ON PROTECTIVE CLOTHING. DO NOT DRINK SOLVENTS/CLEANING
AGENTS. DO NOT SMOKE. DO NOT BREATHE THE FUMES. SOLVENT/CLEANING AGENTS
ARE POISONOUS AND FLAMMABLE. USE THE APPROVED HAND AND EYE PROTECTION
WHEN YOU APPLY THE CLEANING AGENT.<?Pub _newline>IF YOU GET THE CLEANING
AGENT ON YOUR SKIN OR IN YOUR EYES:<?Pub _newline>- FLUSH IT AWAY
WITH CLEAN WATER.<?Pub _newline>- GET MEDICAL AID.</para>
</warning>
<caution><para>USE ONLY SPECIFIED MATERIALS OR THEIR EQUIVALENT. MATERIALS
THAT ARE NOT SPECIFIED CAN DAMAGE THE SURFACE PROTECTION.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DO ALL THE WORK WITH A FULLY CLEAN WORKBENCH, TOOLS
AND PARTS.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DURING THE CLEANING, PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE ACTUATOR,
HARNESS, SWITCH AND TILT LOCK. DRY THE SEAT AFTER ANY CLEANING.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>PROTECT ALL OTHER NOT REQUIRED SURFACES OF ANY CLEANING
AGENT SPLATTER TO NOT AFFECT THEIR MATERIAL PROPERTIES.</para>
</caution>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-001-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Polycarbonate/ABS fairing</title>
<caution><para>CLEANING AGENTS WITH CHLORINATED SOLVENTS, DENATURED
ALCOHOL, ACETONE AND/OR STRONG DETERGENTS WITH HIGH AMMONIA OR ALKALINE
CONTENTS ARE NOT PERMITTED. STEAM CLEANING IS NOT PERMITTED. THE USE
OF ABOVE GIVEN MATERIAL OR PROCEDURE WILL HAVE AN UNWANTED EFFECT
ON THE MATERIAL PROPERTY, THEN IT BECOMES BRITTLE.</para>
</caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Extreme care must be taken in cleaning all plastics. Alcohol
or bleaches based agents will never have to be used to clean any plastic
materials.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Clean all plastic surfaces with a mild soap (pH&lt; 7) and water
solution.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>To mix soap with water and obtain the desired concentration
refer to the strength needed for cleaning purposes.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Apply the solution directly to the surface and rub with a clean
cloth to loosen any dirt and debris.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Rinse with clear water, then wipe off with a dry cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-160-002-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Dress covers</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>All previously stated considerations concerning
dress covers remain in effect. In addition to appearance and sanitary
considerations, the cleanliness of dress covers can affect the thermal
performance of the fire blocking system. Cleaning intervals for dress
covers must be evaluated to ensure against unwanted contamination
build up and transfer of contamination through to the fire blocking
liner.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>The fabric looses it&rsquo;s fire blocking capacity after
twenty washings.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-160-003-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Cushions</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The factors affecting the thermal performance
of cushions are the density of the cushions and theirs cleanliness.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Tests have shown that changes in cushion firmness (IFD
/ Identification Force Deflection) do not affect the thermal performance
properties of the cushion.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Heavy stains on cushions, particularly from petroleum
materials, must not be allowed to build up. Mild non-volatile, non-flammable
cleaners can be used gently on the surface of the cushion. Do not
rub hard enough to break the skin of the foam. Because of the fire
blocking layer, cushions can be expected to remain fairly clean.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-004-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Upholstery Cleaning Procedures (Seat Covers and FBL)</title>
<note><para>For wool fabrics (carpet included), machine cleaning procedure
(washing) must be avoided to prevent shrinkage. Dry cleaning is recommended.
In case of doubt, contact the fabric supplier.</para>
</note>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Machine cleaning procedure</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Identification and classification of the stains.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Examine the covers before cleaning to identify
stains which are not removed by machine cleaning and therefore submit
them to a pre-washing. Machine cleaning can in fact alter these stains
and make their successive elimination quite difficult.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>As general criteria remember that these stains are
not directly removed in the machine, and therefore necessary a pre-washing:
</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>Coca cola, wine, blood, fruit,
sweat, food.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>On the contrary, machine cleaning removes stains
of:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>Coffee, fats, alcoholic drinks,
some kinds of ink.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Generally stains is recognized as follows:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>Coffee and ink stains for
their color and neat outline.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Wine, coca cola, alcoholic drinks and sweat stains
for their extensive and shaded outline.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Food and fat stains for their consistence.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Fruit and blood stains are not easily recognizable.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Pre-washing</para>
<note><para>Pre-washing is advisable for all of stains of uncertain
nature.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Do the pre-washing as follows:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Prepare a mixture of neptune, perchlorethylene, water with a
1: 1: 1 ratio. Quantity: about 1 l (0.2642 US gal) of mixture for
30 covers. Do the pre-washing as described above.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Preparation of covers</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The adhesive stripes of all covers must be
covered to prevent fraying of fabric at the end of the cleaning phase.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Preparation of the machine</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>At least once a day it is necessary to do these
operations.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Regenerate the perchlorethylene through distillation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Add, directly in the reservoir, 1 l (0.2642 US gal) of the pure
additive used in pre-washing to every 100 l (26.42 US gal) of perchlorethylene.
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Washing phase</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Before each load of covers add one of theses
additives to the perchlorethylene, directly in the drum:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Neptune: prepare a mixture of additive, alcohol water in a ratio
of 1: 1: 1, for 1.5 l (0.3963 US gal) of mixture for every 20 kg (44
lbs) of covers to be washed.</para>
<note><para>The additive introduced in the drum must be the same as
the one used for the pre-washing.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Mix the perchlorethylene and the mixture before introducing
the covers, to help the dispersion of the additive in the solvent.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Load the drum with the covers, make sure that the adhesive stripes
are covered. The quantity of covers must not be over 80% of the machine
maximum operation load.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Wash for five minutes at room temperature.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Spin for 3 minutes, do not exceed 500 r.p.m.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Rinse for 5 minutes with pure solvent at room temperature.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Dry the covers, do not exceed the temperature of 60&deg;C (140&deg;F).
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Control and repetition of treatment</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Examine the covers, one by one, to separate
those which still have stains. Pre-wash again the covers which still
present stains per steps (2) 2) and 3). Machine wash them together
with another load of the same type. The second pre-wash is essential
to prevent the stain becoming even more resistant to removal.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Ironing and final control</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The covers which have not been rejected must
be ironed and must subjected to a more accurate control, to select
and return to the cycle those still having stains.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Dry cleaning procedure</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cover all hook (male) auto agrip tapes with their counterpart
(loop tape) to prevent any damages to the fabric during the dry cleaning
procedure.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Spray the covers with a detergent activator and left for about
20 min before loaded to the dry cleaning machine. Slightly brushed
heavily stained areas with a soft brush.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the dry cleaning procedure, please follow the instructions
of the machine supplier.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>About 70 to 80% of the covers became clean during pre-treatment
and dry cleaning-depending on the cleaning system and kind of stains.
The spots still disable can be cleaner with a steam gun and then dry
cleaning again. Before loaded to be dry cleaning machine, the fabric
must be fully dry to prevent shrinkage.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="403"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-403-A01">
<tgroup cols="2"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec
colname="col3" colwidth="1.00*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry namest="col1" nameend="col3" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont
Weight="bold">
<para>Cleaning Materials</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.39in">
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Stain</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>What to Use</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Alcohol, Liquors</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use shampoo and then mop with denatured alcohol.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Beer</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with tepid water (50 &deg;C max. (122 &deg;F max.)) with 3% denatured alcohol.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.39in">
<entry>
<para>Blood</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with cold water,  then shampoo and use 5% ammonia.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Butter, Oil, Sauce</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with ethyl alcohol and perchlorethylene. Use shampoo and then 5% ammonia, if stain remains.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Chewing-gum</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with acetone or perchlorethylene.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Chocolate</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with tepid water (50 &deg;C  max. (122 &deg;F max.)) or with 5% ammonia.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Coffee, Tea</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use shampoo and denatured alcohol or 10% ammonia if stain remains.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Egg</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with 5% ammonia or denatured alcohol, then use shampoo.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Fruits, Food</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with tepid water and then use shampoo.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Glue, Paints</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use ethyl alcohol or perchlorethylene. then mop with tepid water or shampoo.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Grass, Vegetables</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Moisten with denatured alcohol.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Ink, Coal</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use absorbent paper, then mop with a solution of 30% denatured alcohol and 70% water. Use also lemon juice.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Juice, Jam</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with tepid water (50 &deg;C max. (122 &deg;F max.)), if stain remains use ethyl alcohol or perchlorethylene.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Mayonnaise, Ketchup, Mustard</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use 10% ammonia and perchlorethylene. Then use shampoo.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Milk, Ice cream, Cream</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use shampoo then mop with 5% ammonia or perchlorethylene.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Mud</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Let it dry up and then use vacuum-cleaner.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Shoe polish, Floor, Wax</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use ethyl alcohol or perchlorethylene. If stain remains use 5% ammonia or denatured alcohol.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Sugar</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with tepid water and then use shampoo.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Tar</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with denatured alcohol or perchlorethylene, then use shampoo.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Vomit, Urine, Ordures</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Mop with water and 50% vinegar or denatured alcohol, then use shampoo.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Water</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Absorb with a cleaned cloth and let it dry up. Use shampoo or alcohol on eventual rings.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Wax, Paraffin</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Put on the seat absorbent paper and iron it. Mop with perchlorethylene and then use shampoo.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Wine, Drinks</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Use a solution of 50% vinegar and then shampoo.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-005-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Metal parts</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Moisten a clean, dry cloth with dry cleaning
solvent and thoroughly, wipe metal parts fully clean. Repeat as required
to remove the stubborn accumulations of dirt and grease. Dry with
a fresh, clean and dry cloth.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-006-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Fabric-backed vinyl</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>KEEP CLEANING SOLVENT AWAY FROM SPARKS OR OPEN FLAMES.
prevent BREATHE FUMES OR long CONTACT OF SOLVENT WITH SKIN supply
sufficient airflow.</para>
</warning>
<unlist><unlitem><para>This type of material is cleaned with a mild
soap and water solution such as Ivory liquid soap and wiped clean
and dry. Do not use solvent-type cleaners.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-007-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Leathers</title>
<revst>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Clean with a water-based, pH-neutral soap or cleaner (no alcohol
or other solvents).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Do not use detergents or solvent-type cleaners.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The cloth used must be only slightly dampened with the soapy
solution.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>After cleaning, it is possible to rinse the surface using a
separate cloth slightly moistened with water only.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The leather must be allowed to air dry naturally; accelerated
drying methods such as hair dryers must not be used.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
<revend></subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-008-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Cleaning requirements for actuators</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Use chlorinated solvent and lint-free cloth to clean the mechanical
parts except for ball bearing, actuator screw and pinions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Dry with compressed air.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Wipe grease in excess on ball bearing, actuator screw and pinions
with dry, lint-free cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put components in a dry clean container to prevent from dirt
or other damage.</para>
<note><para>Cleaning must be done in clean and with sufficient airflow
premises. All standard precautions must be taken with chlorinated
solvents.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-009-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Twin material cover (if applicable)</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Twin fabric / leather cover</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Fabric: Clean manually and separately by spray extraction (steam
and vacuum) after protection of the leather.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para><revst>Leather: Clean with a water-based, pH-neutral soap or
cleaner (no alcohol or other solvents). Do not use detergents or solvent-type
cleaners.<revend></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Twin fabric / carpet cover</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Fabric and carpet: dry cleaning is recommended.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Twin leather / carpet cover</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para><revst>Leather: Clean with a water-based, pH-neutral soap or
cleaner (no alcohol or other solvents). Do not use detergents or solvent-type
cleaners.<revend></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Carpet: Clean manually and separately by spray extraction (steam
and vacuum) after protection of leather.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-160-010-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Restraint cleaning guidelines</title>
<warning><para>BEFORE YOU USE A CLEANING MATERIAL, YOU MUST KNOW THE
HAZARD CODE AND get THE NECESSARY PROTECTION REFER TO THE PAGE ABOUT
HAZARD CODES FOR MATERIALS IN THE FRONT RESTRAINT CMM.</para>
</warning>
<caution><para>THE RESTRAINT SYSTEM MUST NOT BE MACHINE-WASHED, BECAUSE
THE WEBBING WILL SHRINK AND ITS PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS WILL BE
CHANGED SIGNIFICANTLY.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>THE RESTRAINT SYSTEM can CLEANED. HOWEVER, THE WEBBING
WILL LOSE ITS ABRASION-RESISTANCE COATING AFTER EACH CLEANING AND
ITS SERVICE LIFE WILL THEREFORE BE DECREASED.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>REFER TO THE CHECK SECTION OF THIS MANUAL TO DETERMINE
WHEN THE WEBBING OF A RESTRAINT SYSTEM MUST BE REPLACED BY AM- SAFE
OR AN AM-SAFE APPROVED REPAIR STATION.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>When CLEANING THE RESTRAINT SYSTEM, precaution MUST
BE TAKEN TO KEEP AWAY FOREIGN MATTER AND CLEANING MEDIA FROM THE HARDWARE
Assemblies.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE SOAP OR WATER ON METAL PARTS.</para>
</caution>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Task definition</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>To clean the Restraint System, remove dirt and unwanted oil
and grease. This helps the Restraint System to last longer and prevents
corrosion of the metal parts. The webbing is to be cleaned with fresh
water and a mild soap. The metal fittings are cleaned with a cloth
moistened with isopropyl alcohol. After cleaning the assemblies, prevent
them from moisture, dirt or other contamination. Keep them protected
until you do a visual check and return the Restraint System to service.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Procedure</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cleaning the webbing</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Attach pieces of cloth to cover the metal fittings.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Wash the webbing: gentle scrub with a soft brush and cold soapy
solution is permissible.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Dry the Restraint System in an area that has a good flow of
air.</para>
<note><para>Do not dry the Restraint System in sunlight or near any
source of heat.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Examine the dry Restraint System. </para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<warning><para>WHEN USING ISOPROPYL ALCOHOL, FOLLOW THe DIRECTIONS
AND WARNINGS GIVEN BY THE MANUFACTURER. PREVENT ANY CONTACT WITH THE
WEBBING MATERIAL.</para>
</warning>
<para>Cleaning hardware</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<title>Clean the hardware with a lint-free cloth moistened with isopropyl
alcohol.</title>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="160" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-160-011-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Seat covers, Curtains and Genuine leather</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>General consideration</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>This documentation is based on Lantal present
knowledge / experience and is intended to provide general information
on their products and their uses. It should therefore not be interpreted
as guaranteeing specific properties of the products or their suitability
for a particular application. The documentation is a recommendation
and is not legally binding.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Please do not hesitate to contact holger.dozsa@lantal.ch
for further information.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Wool - Wool blend - Mohair velvet: Seat covers / Curtains (pleated
and nonpleated)</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Sorting</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Sort curtains and seat covers separately.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Precaution</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>All hook (male) Velcro tapes must be covered
with their counterpart - loop tape - to avoid any damage to the fabric
during the dry cleaning process. Furthermore, we recommend to fix
pleated curtains made of wool in a frame to avoid the dissolving of
the pleats. <?Pub _newline>MOHAIR velour = P.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Pre-treatment</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>We recommend to spray the spots with a detergent
activator and left for about 20 minutes before loaded into the dry
cleaning machine. Heavily stained areas should be slightly brushed
with a soft brush.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Dry cleaning</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>For the dry cleaning process, please follow
the instructions of the machine supplier.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Re-treatment</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>About 70 to 80 % of the covers should become
clean during pre-treatment and dry cleaning - depending on the cleaning
system and kind of stains. The spots still visible can be cleaned
with a steam gun followed by another dry-cleaning cycle. Before it
is loaded into the dry cleaning machine, the fabric must be completely
dry to avoid shrinkage.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Fabrics cleaned in accordance with our recommendations
can be dry cleaned up to 20 times without losing the flame-resistant
properties.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>You will find suppliers of dry cleaning machines
and cleaning detergents on a separate list.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Polyester (Trevira CS): Seat covers / Curtains (pleated and
non-pleated)</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Sorting</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Sort curtains and seat covers separately. Pleated
curtains have been processed to receive a permanent set to the pleat
edges and fabric weave. To minimize stretching and distortion, it
is important that pleated curtains are placed in net bags for washing.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Washing</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The most suitable appliances are the small
"all-in-one" machines with a capacity up to 60 kg (132.27 lbs). The
machine should only be loaded with 1/3 of its capacity. All hook (male)
Velcro tapes must be covered by their counterpart &ndash; loop tape
- to avoid any damage to the fabric during washing. Please follow
the instructions of the machine supplier.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="404"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-404-A01">
<tgroup cols="5">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="1823.00px">
<colspec colname="col1" colwidth="0.99*"><colspec colname="col2"
colwidth="0.91*"><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.07*"><colspec
colname="col4" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec colname="col5" colwidth="1.03*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="bottom"></entry>
<entry valign="bottom">
<para>Liquor Ratio</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="bottom">
<para>Water Temperature</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="bottom">
<para>Additives</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="bottom">
<para>Process Time</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.63in">
<entry morerows="1">
<para><?Pub _font Weight="bold">First Wash<?Pub /_font></para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>1:7 to 1:8</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Up to 30&deg;C (86&deg;F)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>20-35 g/kg (0.32-0.56 oz/lb) non-ionic detergent</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>10 to 15 min</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.63in">
<entry></entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><?Pub _font Weight="bold">Interim Rinse<?Pub /_font></para>
<para>If the curtains are very dirty we recommend an intermediate rinse</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>1:7 to 1:8</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Up to 30&deg;C (86&deg;F)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>10 ml/kg (0.16 oz.fl./lb) chlorine bleach (15% solution)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>5 to 10 min</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><?Pub _font Weight="bold">Main Wash<?Pub /_font></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>1:7 to 1:8</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Normal Wash 30&deg;- 40&deg;C (86&deg;F - 104&deg;F) use soft water
</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Normal Wash 10-15 g/kg (0.16-0.24 oz/lb) non-ionic detergent</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Approx. 10 min.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><?Pub _font Weight="bold">Rinse<?Pub /_font></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>1:8 in hard water</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Cool slowly to about 20&deg;C (68&deg;F) in order to avoid temperature shock and creasing
</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>It is not recommended to use fabric conditioners as the flame retardant properties may be adversely affected.
</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>-</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><?Pub _font Weight="bold">Spinning<?Pub /_font></para>
</entry>
<entry namest="col2" nameend="col5">
<para>Light spin leaving residual moisture content of approx. 30-50%</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><?Pub _font Weight="bold">Drying<?Pub /_font></para>
</entry>
<entry namest="col2" nameend="col5">
<para>Hang curtain to dry straight after machine washing. Tumble drying is also possible. Load at a ratio of no more than 1/3 of usual load. Dry at maximum of 70&deg;C (158&deg;F) waste air temperature and retain in an air-ventilated rotary drum until completely cool.
</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Genuine leather</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>LANTAL GENUINE LEATHER IS TREATED WITH A LIGHT TINTED
COAT OF VARNISH TO ENHANCE THE FUNCTIONALITY OF THE LEATHER, MAKING
IT LIGHT FAST, WATER- AND OIL-REPELLENT AND PERMEABLE TO STEAM. DON&rsquo;T
USE ANY DETERGENTS!</para>
</caution>
<para>Interim cleaning</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>For the interim cleaning we recommend the use
of a mild soap solution applied by a sponge or a soft cloth. Then
wipe off the soap water with fresh water and dry with a soft cloth.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Main cleaning</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>This is a deep cleaning intervention using cleaning fluids for
leather. Wet a sponge with the cleaner and clean the leather with
circular movements. Don&rsquo;t rub! Dry up gently with a clean cloth
and let dry for at least 30 minutes.</para>
<note><para>We recommend the exclusive use of the cleaning products
(see separate list) because these products have been tested on Lantal
genuine leather.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="5001" chg="u"
key="PGBLK-25-15-65-5001-" revdate="20250131">
<title>CHECK</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="200" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-200-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Check</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Reason for the job</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Use standard industry procedures to do a visual
check of all visible parts for cracks, defects, or damage.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Defective or damaged items must be replaced with serviceable
items.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Conduct checks under a bright light. Use a
5X to 7X power magnifying glass to detect surface flaws.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Replace, with a serviceable part, any part that fails
to meet the requirements of check. If defective part is repairable,
note defect and assign part for repair.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Dents or other damage must not impair finish or functional
operation of any part.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Proper reassembly and adjustment of a Seat Assembly
precludes any additional checks.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>However, prior to disassembly or following any significant
repair, do the following check as applicable.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tools, features and equipment</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="501"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-501-A01">
<tgroup cols="3"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="1.00*"><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.00*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Reference</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Qty</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Designation</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Standard mechanics technician's tool.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>No specific</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left">
<para>As Required</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>5X to 7X power magnifying glass.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Consumables</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<numlist>
<numlitem><para>Not applicable.</para></numlitem>
</numlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>If repair of the equipment assembly is necessary, <refint
reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-6001-">(refer to Page Block 6001)
&ldquo;REPAIR&rdquo;</refint>.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>If overhaul of the equipment assembly or a
sub-assembly of the seat, shell or monument are required, <refint
reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-5001-">(refer to Page Block 5001)
&ldquo;CHECK&rdquo;</refint>, paragraph "Entry in service after storage"
and if necessary <refint reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-6001-">(refer
to Page Block 6001) &ldquo;REPAIR&rdquo;</refint>, chapter have to
be used as applicable workscope.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Referenced information</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="502"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-502-A01">
<tgroup cols="2"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.10*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="0.90*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Reference</para>
</entry>
<entry align="left"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Designation</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-870-804-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Dimensions</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-810-801-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Testing and fault isolation</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-870-801-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Description and operation</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-300-801-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Repair</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para><refint reftype="task" refid="Task-25-15-65-940-801-A01"></refint></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Fits and clearances</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><title>Procedure</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Inspection/Check</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Visually examine that all parts are clean and free of cracks,
corrosion, deterioration, and obvious signs of damage.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine security of all clamps and straps securing leads and
all other parts not removed during disassembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Visually examine all threaded parts for crossed or damaged threads.
Reject part if thread damage exceeds 50% of one thread.</para>
<note><para>If damage to any one thread is 50% or less, note defect
and assign part for repair.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine sewn seams for fraying or separation and fabric for
fraying, scuffing and rips.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine attaching bolts, nuts, screws and pins for tightness
and floor attaching fittings for wear or deformation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine helicoil inserts for damage and security of installation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine structural parts including clips, brackets and machined
parts for damage, cracks and sharp nicks.</para>
<note><para>Burrs are defined as material raised above the normal
surface, which if not removed would prevent complete and proper mating
of parts and sealing surfaces. Where nicks or scratches allow bare
metal to show through a protective finish, note defect and assign
part for repair. Dents or other damage must not impair finish or functional
operation of any part.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine paint and finishes for chipping and worn spots, and
note condition of bonding on parts and assemblies.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine nameplate and placards for legibility and secure attachment.
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cushions are recommended to be replaced at three years interval
to guarantee maximum comfort.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Pre-flight checks</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine seat general status (leather and sheepskin upholstering).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine proper operation of seat translation. Make sure that
there is nothing interfere between the seat track and the seat. Make
sure that the seat track locking pins ensure correctly the seat stop
while pushing aft / forward the seat. If it is not the case, remove
the seat to clean the locking pins and the seat track.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine proper electrical up and down seat operation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine the armrest control for correct operation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine proper manual up and down seat operation (Use handcrank).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine proper seat belt attach.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine the tilt position of the backrest.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine the longitudinal adjustment.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine the lateral adjustment.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Examine thigh rest system.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Restore the seat to normal position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Recommended Scheduled Checks</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Conduct recommended scheduled checks in accordance
with <refint reftype="1" refid="Table-25-15-65-997-501-A01">Table
25-15-65-997-501-A01</refint> (If Applicable).</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>Examine all adjustment detailed in <refint reftype="1"
refid="TASK-25-15-65-940-801-A01">TASK 25-15-65-940-801-A01 "FITS
AND CLEARANCES" (Refer to Page Block 8001)</refint>.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
