<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Restraint system</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para> First of all make sure that the restraint
system is clean.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Harness</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that every component of the harness is correctly attached.
Each elements must lock on the buckle.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that strand belt is not caught when the loop is activated.
No elements must get caught.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the two mounting screws are on the pelvis straps
(1 per side) and the inertia reels screws correctly tightened. Fasteners
must pivot.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the dorsal wires are wound correctly to stop
(guide strap) with a consistent speed. The necessary time for the
rolling-up of belts between maxi deployment and propped up over guides
belts must be included between 1 and 2 seconds.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the ventral strands adjusters is working correctly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Fittings</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure burrs, nicks or scratches, cracks, dents and corrosion.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Rotary buckle and connectors</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure burrs, nicks or scratches, cracks, dents and corrosion.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Reel assembly</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Make sure burrs, nicks or scratches, cracks, dents and corrosion.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Miscellaneous</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Discard of rollers<?Pub _newline><grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-501-a01"></grphcref></para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>The rollers need to be changed every 6000 FH to ensure a reliable
longitudinal movement of the seat along the seat track.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para> For removal and installation procedure <refint reftype="PGBLK"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-3001-"></refint> and <refint reftype="PGBLK"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-7001-"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="501"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-501-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Discard
of Rollers</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-501-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-501-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Preventive maintenance for actuation system P/N F0445552</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>The inspection interval can vary with aircraft usage and each
airlines.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>The recommended inspection interval for that follows must be
less than six months:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>Electrically operate the electrical
actuator. It must run smoothly and quietly, stopping when the command
switch is released or at the designed end of travel.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examine the manual override by turning the override
shaft with a handle crank. It must run smoothly without excessive
force.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Visually examine to make sure that the electrical actuator
mounting is attached at both ends of the electrical actuator, and
that it is free to move about the pivots.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Make sure that electrical connectors are installed
properly and fully engaged with the locking ring tight.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examine ground strap connection. Tighten if necessary.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examine electrical cables for evidence of wear, cut
and connector damage.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examine the electrical actuator housing for evidence
of cracks or other physical damage that can be detrimental to operation.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>If any of the checks is not correct, electrical actuator
or wiring harness must be replaced.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Maintenance records</para>
<note><para>Invalid maintenance records could void warranty.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="PGBLK-25-15-65-6001-" revdate="20250131">
<title>REPAIR</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="300" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-300-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Repair</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Reason for the job</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>Tolerance of scratches, cuts, nicks, dents, etc., on
plastic and other components is established by the airline's own standards
for aircraft interiors.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Replace cracked plastic components; they are considered
"not repairable".</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Replace damaged metal components; they are considered
"not repairable".</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>In case of seats component of seat structure and their
attachment to each other are not repairable.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Burrs, nicks and scratches are defined as any material
lifted above the surface of the part. Minor burrs, nicks and scratches
must be polished. Be careful to not impair form, fit or function. <?Pub
_newline>Surface layer must be replaced after polish. Cracks are not
permitted.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tools, features and equipment</para>
<note><para>See Chapter <refint reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-3001-">
&ldquo;DISASSEMBLY&rdquo;</refint> <refint reftype="0"
refid="Table-25-15-65-997-301-A01"> - Tools List</refint>.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Consumables<?Pub _newline></para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>USE ALL ADHESIVES AND REPAIR MATERIALS IN AN AREA WITH
GOOD AIRFLOW. DO NOT BREATHE FUMES OR LET THE ADHESIVES AND REPAIR
MATERIALS CONTACT THE SKIN. OBEY ALL INSTRUCTIONS AND HEALTH AND SAFETY
WARNINGS SUPPLIED BY THE MANUFACTURER. OBEY ALL APPLICABLE FIRE PRECAUTIONS.
THIS WILL HELP PREVENT INJURY.</para>
</warning>
<warning><para>MAKE SURE PROTECTIVE CLOTHING AND EYE PROTECTION ARE
USED OR INJURY CAN OCCUR.</para>
</warning>
<caution><para>ALL THE CONSUMABLES SUPPLIED BY SAFRAN AND LISTED INTO
THE CMM can HAVE A LIMITED LIFETIME. PLEASE REVIEW LABELS ON CONTAINER
OR EXAMINE THE TECHNICAL DATA SHEET BEFORE use OR STORE.</para>
</caution>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para></para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>You can use equivalent alternatives for items in the lists.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
