</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><title>Procedure</title>
<note><para>In addition to the following details, the operators could
use the FAA standard AC43-13 &ldquo;Permitted procedures, techniques
and practices - Aircraft Inspection and repair&rdquo; as permitted
minor repair procedures after being submitted to Safran Seats (Safran
Seats France) then approved.</para>
</note>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-001-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Scouring</title>
<warning><para>USE SYDOL SID WITH RUBBER GLOVES AND GLASSES IN ONE
AREA WITH SUFFICIENT AIRFLOW.</para>
</warning>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Scour paint from the metal parts, use SYDOL
SID.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-002-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Protection</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Clean thoroughly each part before application.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Use the masking tape to prevent damage to the unpainted zones.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-003-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Auto agrip</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>In the event that any auto agrip which is bonded to metal or
plastic has come loose it must be replaced. For best results remove
the entire piece, clean the exposed surface <refint reftype="1"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-4001-">(Refer to "CLEANING", paragraph D "PROCEDURE")
</refint> and wipe dry with clean cotton cloth. To install a new piece
of auto agrip refer to manufacturers instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="d"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-004-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Deleted</title>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-005-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Corrosion and protection:</title>
<caution><para>BE CAREFUL NOT TO DAMAGE THE CORRODED PART BY A TOO
IMPORTANT SANDING.</para>
</caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Corrosion elimination:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Sand lightly the corroded surfaces with an
abrasive paper (grit P 600), until the corrosion has fully disappear.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>If necessary use an abrasive paper (grit P 400) or
less.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Treated surfaces protection:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Use an anti-corrosive film (ex. ARDROX 396/1)
to prevent damage on sanded surfaces.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-006-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Thread fasteners securing:</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Apply the Loctite No. 222, 243, 262 or 270 to all non self locking
thread fasteners.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<revst>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>For inserts on plastic parts, ensure the Loctite does not spread
beyond the threads and seep onto the plastic as it could weaken the
material.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
<revend></subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="11" subjnbr="58" func="350" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-350-007-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Small Areas of Damaged Paint Repair (Painted surface)</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>General</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>The repair scheme shown below is intended for repairs to small
areas of damaged paint of less than 5806.44 sq mm [9.00 sq in] area
and isolated from other areas of damaged by at least 304.80 mm [12.00
in]. It is possible that the finished repair will not be to the initial
production quality standard.</para>
<note><para>For larger repairs refer to Safran Seats France.</para>
</note>
<note><para>This repair is for small areas of damaged paint contained
in a maximum area of 76.2 mm x 76.2 mm (3 in x 3 in). The damaged
paint must be a minimum of 304.80 mm (12 in) away from other areas
of damage. For larger repairs contact Safran Seats France.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Procedure</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>DO ALL PAINT/LACQUER SPRAY-GUN PROCEDURES IN AN AREA
WITH GOOD AIRFLOW. DO NOT BREATHE PAINT/ SOLVENT FUMES AND USE MANUFACTURER&rsquo;S
RECOMMENDED BREATHING MASKS AND EQUIPMENT. OBEY HEALTH AND SAFETY
WARNING RECOMMENDED BY THE MANUFACTURER AND THE LOCAL HEALTH AND SAFETY
REGULATOR. OBEY APPLICABLE FIRE PRECAUTIONS. THIS WILL HELP PREVENT
INJURY.</para>
</warning>
<warning><para>WHEN YOU USE CLEANING AGENTS, OBEY THE MANUFACTURER&rsquo;S
INSTRUCTIONS.</para>
</warning>
<caution><para>WHEN YOU USE FILLERS, PRIMERS AND PAINTS, OBEY THE
MANUFACTURER&rsquo;S INSTRUCTIONS.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT CLEAN THE REPAIRED AREA FOR 48 HOURS.</para>
</caution>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Remove paint back to the surface of the material.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Prepare surface to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Apply a layer of filler, refer to <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-601-A01">Assembly of colors</refint>,
to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Prepare surface to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Apply a layer of primer, refer to <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-601-A01">Assembly of colors</refint>,
to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Prepare surface to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Apply a layer of top coat paint, refer to <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-601-A01">Assembly of colors</refint>,
to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Finish surface to the paint manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-008-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Assembly of colors</title>
