<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-350-009-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Riveted assemblies</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>DO NOT DRILL FULLY THROUGH THE RIVET SLEEVE TO REMOVE
A RIVET AS THIS WILL TEND TO MAKE THE HOLE LARGER.</para>
</caution>
<para>Removal of the rivet</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>It is recommended that a small center drill be used to provide
a guide for a larger drill on top of the rivet, and the upper portion
of the stem be drilled away to destroy the lock <grphcref
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01"> </grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Drive out the rivet stem with a tapered steel drift pin, or
spent stem <grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01"> </grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Drill nearly through the head of the rivet with a drill the
same size as the rivet shank <grphcref
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01"> </grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Break off rivet head with a drift pin as a pry <grphcref
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01"> </grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Drive out the remaining rivet shank with a pin having a diameter
equal to the rivet shank <grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01"></grphcref>.
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Installation of the rivet</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Before install the new rivets, examine the
size of the hole to determine if the original fastener size may be
reinstalled or if an oversize fastener will be required.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Use the aircraft structural repair manual or FAA document
EA-AC65-15A, &ldquo;Airframe and Powerplant Mechanics Handbook&rdquo;
to make this determination and install the new fastener in accordance
with these documents.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Removal of the rivet (secondary structure only)</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>If removal of any solid rivet is necessary,
accomplish the work in accordance with the aircraft structural repair
manual or FAA document EA-AC5-15A, &ldquo;Airframe and Powerplant
Mechanics Handbook&rdquo;.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>If removal of any blind rivet is necessary, accomplish
the work in accordance with the preceding recommended procedure,<grphcref
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01"></grphcref> (&ldquo;1&rdquo;
thru &ldquo;5&rdquo;).</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="602" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-602-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Riveted
Assemblies</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-602-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-602-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="11" subjnbr="58" func="350" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-350-010-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Helicoil Installation</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Insertion of thread insert</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>The installation can be done manually, automatically or with
machine tools. The HELICOIL is screwed onto the installation mandrel
with the tang down (a), inserted into the leader cartridge (b) or
placed on the flyover tool (c). Then, the tool is placed over the
tapped hole.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="603"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-603-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Helicoil
Installation (1)</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-603-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-603-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Installation</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>By turning the threaded mandrel (d), the mandrel (e) or the
fly-over tool (f), respectively, manually or triggering the drive,
the thread insert is screwed in. It must be installed at least 1/4
Thread pitch below the top surface.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="604"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-604-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Helicoil
Installation (2)</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-604-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-604-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Breaking off the tang</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>To produce a through-hole thread, the tang is broken off at
the notch. For that, a tang break-off tool is used (g and h). For
threads from M 14 (fine and normal pitch), the tang can be removed
with long nose pliers (i).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="605"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-605-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Helicoil
Installation (3)</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-605-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-605-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="11" subjnbr="58" func="350" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-350-011-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Rivnut Removal and Installation Procedures (SIL 0006)</title>
<grphcref refid="Graphic-25-15-65-991-606-A01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Removal procedure of rivnuts with cylinder and countersunk head
shapes.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>SHOULD BE CAREFUL NOT TO MAKE THE EXISTING HOLE BIGGER.</para>
</caution>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>With a drill bit of 6.1 mm (0.24 in) (for rivnut
thread size 6/32 or 8/32) and 7.1 mm (0.28) for rivnut thread size
10/32, drill slowly by making circular movements to cut and remove
the rivnut head.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Installation procedure of rivnuts with cylinder and countersunk
head shapes.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>EXAMINE THAT THE CORRECT SIZE PULL-UP STUD IS INSTALLED
IN THE HEADER DEPENDING UPON THE RIVNUT THREAD SIZE.</para>
</caution>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Place new rivnut head-first on the pull-up
stud of the manual tool and screw till the anvil. Follow supplier
manual for more details.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>The required pull-up stud(s) shall be procured from the
tool supplier depending upon the rivnut thread size.</para>
</note>
<note><para>If the pull-up stud needs to be changed, follow the steps
given in the tool supplier manual.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The rivnut head shall be in touch with the
anvil and the pull-up stud shall be flush with the rivnut open end.
Follow supplier manual if adjustment is required.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Place the tool with the rivnut in the hole
and press firmly the handle according to install the rivnut.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Upon releasing the handle, the tool will be
released from the rivnut. Follow supplier manual for more details.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>Tool represented for illustration.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="606"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" chg="u" key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-606-A01"
revdate="20250131"><title>Rivnut Removal and Installation</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-606-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-606-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
