<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="350" seq="012"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Subtask-25-15-65-350-012-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Damaged Screw Removal (SIL 0019)</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15"
subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="607" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="6001" chg="u" key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-607-A01"
revdate="20250131"><title>Examples of Damaged Screws</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-607-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-607-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Remove the damaged head by drilling or milling or filling it.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Drill a hole into the remaining screw <grphcref
refid="Graphic-25-15-65-991-607-A01"></grphcref>.</para>
<note><para>Drill with a drill bit having a diameter smaller than
the thread diameter.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Mount a screw extractor fitted on an screwing machine.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Set the screwing machine to a slow speed and high torque.</para>
<note><para>Consult the screw extractor instructions for speed and
torque value if indicated.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Screw slowly the extractor into the screw while applying pressure
to extract it <grphcref refid="Graphic-25-15-65-991-609-A01"></grphcref><grphcref
refid="Graphic-25-15-65-991-610-A01">and </grphcref>.</para>
<note><para>The extractor is turned counter-clockwise to screw it.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>If the extractor do not extract the screw, go back from step
(b) and drill a hole one size bigger.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Clean the part and remove any particle of screw.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Examine the thread of the part to ensure it is not damaged before
a new screw is installed.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="608" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-608-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Damaged
Screw Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-608-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-608-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="609" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-609-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Damaged
Screw Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-609-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-609-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="610" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6001" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-610-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Damaged
Screw Removal</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-610-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-610-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="PGBLK-25-15-65-7001-" revdate="20250131">
<title>ASSEMBLY</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="400" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-400-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Assembly</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Reason for the job</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>This chapter contains the instructions to do the assembly
of the Equipment.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="none">
<unlitem><para>Before assembly, verify that <refint reftype="1"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-4001-">(refer to Page Block 4001) "CLEANING"</refint>, <refint
reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-5001-">(refer to Page Block 5001)
"CHECK"</refint> and <refint reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-6001-">(refer
to Page Block 6001) "REPAIR"</refint> of all component parts have
been carried out.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para> After repair or replacement of any damaged or worn
parts, reassemble the Equipment following accepted workshop practices,
noting the following detailed instructions. Use a tracking fixture
to support the seat structure.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Refer to the illustrations in the Illustrated Parts
List for location, sequence, quantity and identification of assemblies,
sub-assemblies and parts. These illustrations are also intended as
a guide line for the assembly procedure.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Replace systematically the self-locking nuts and pins
after a dismantling operation.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>To prevent errors during assembly, refer to the marking
or numbering of the component parts.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tools, features and equipment</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="992" seq="701"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" id="TABLE-25-15-65-992-701-A01">
