</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Not applicable.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Procedure</title>
<note><para>In order to prevent errors during assembly, refer to the
marking or numbering of the component parts. Following the replacement
of worn or damaged parts assemble the seat as follows:</para>
</note>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-001-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Rollers</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-701-A01"> </grphcref>
<caution><para>DO NOT APPLY GREASE AROUND THE ROLLERS AND THE SEAT
TRACKS.</para>
</caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the new roller with the spacer.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tighten the screw (30) of the roller (20).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15"
subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="701" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="7001" chg="u" key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-701-A01"
revdate="20250131"><title>Installation of Rollers</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-701-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-701-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-002-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Seat Pan</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-702-A01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Engage the seat pan on the lower structure.</para>
<note><para>The spacers (60) must be mounted between the seat pan
and the lower structure. Attach seat pan on lower structure with shafts
(30), spacers (60), washers (40), washers (45),  and nuts (50).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Connect the electrical actuator, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-007-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the seat pan fairings, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="702" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-702-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Cables, Adjustment and Test</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-702-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-702-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-003-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Armrest</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-703-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Position armrest equipped.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Attach with screw (90), washer (100), spacer (110) and nut (120).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Clip the armcap (70).</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="703" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-703-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Armrest</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-703-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-703-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-004-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Backrest on Seat Pan</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-704-A01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put backrest (140) on seat pan.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Attach backrest with shafts (140), washers (150) and nuts (160).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Connect hydrolocks head control, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-007-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Re-install mechanical command of restraint system, <refint
reftype="SUBTASK" refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-008-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Re-install all cables removal, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-006-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the seat pan fairings, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="704" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-704-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Backrest on Seat Pan</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-704-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-704-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-005-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Tilt Hydrolock and Control</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-705-A01"> </grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install hydrolock on backrest with screw (230), washer (240)
and nut (250).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Attach shaft (210) and washer (220).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Connect the hydrolock head control (130) by screw (140).</para>
<note><para>Before installing the hydrolock, make sure that it is
in the fully extended position.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the seat pan fairings, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="705" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-705-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Tilt Hydrolock and Control</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-705-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-705-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-006-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Cables, Adjustment and Test</title>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-950-804-A01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-706-A01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-707-A01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-708-A01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-709-A01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-710-A01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-711-A01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>IF THE CABLE IS NOT IN THE CORRECT POSITION IT CAN
GET SQUEEZED AT THE CONTROL HANDLE MECHANISM, THE BACKREST HINGE OR
THE LOWER STRUCTURE.</para>
</caution>
<para>Install the new lateral front control cables (20) and (30A)
as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Pass the new lateral front control cables <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-706-A01">(Refer to item 20 and item 30A,
Fig. 7006)</refint> as the yellow and green cable <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-707-A01"> (Refer to Fig. 7007)</refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach a nut (230) on the lateral front control cable threading
(20) or (30A).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the lateral front control cable threading (20) or (30A)
on the holding bracket (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach a nut (230) on the lateral front control cable threading
(20) or (30A) after the holding bracket (280). </para>
<note><para>Make sure that 20 mm (0.78 in) of the threading remain
visible.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Put the lower end of the lateral front control cables (20) and
(30A) in the hole of the cap (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the circlips (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Put the assembly (40), (80) and (90) in position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the control pin (100) with Loctite n&deg;242.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the two screws (105) of the cap (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Tighten the two screws (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the cable stop (210) on the handle (290) and attach
it with cotter pin (220).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the cable clamps to attach the new lateral front control
cables (20) and (30A) to the seat pan.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the new tilt control cable (50) attached with the control
pin (100) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Pass the new tilt control cable <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-706-A01">(item 50, Fig. 7006)</refint> as
the blue cables <refint reftype="0" refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-707-A01"></refint>.
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach a nut (230) on the tilt control cable (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the tilt control cable (50) on the holding bracket (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach a nut (230) on the tilt control cable (50) after the
holding bracket (280).</para>
<note><para>The cable threading end must be against the holding bracket.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Insert each control lever of the cables (90) onto each backrest
hydrolock (200).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Tighten the screw (140) of the hydrolocks (200) with an allen
key.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cable divider (100) to the backrest structure with
the cable clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the cable stop (210) on the handle (290) attached with
the cotter pin (220).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the new tilt control cable (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the new longitudinal LH and RH control cable (10) as
follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Pass the new longitudinal LH and RH control cable <refint
reftype="1" refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-706-A01">(Refer to item 10,
Fig. 7006)</refint> as the purple cables <refint reftype="0"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-707-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach a nut (230) on the longitudinal LH and RH control cable
(10).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the longitudinal LH and RH control cable (10) on the
holding bracket (280).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach a nut (230) on the longitudinal LH and RH control cable
(10) after the holding bracket (280).</para>
<note><para>Make sure that 20 mm (0.78 in) of the threading remain
visible.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Put the lower end of the longitudinal LH &amp; RH control cable
(10) in the hole of the cap (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the circlips (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Put the assembly (40), (80) and (90) in position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the front control pin (100) with Loctite n&deg;242.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the two screws (105) of the cap (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Tighten the two screws (105).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the cable stop (210) on the handle (290) and attach
it with cotter pin (220).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the cable clamps to attach the new longitudinal LH &amp;
RH control cable (10) to the seat pan.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the new control handle spring as follows <refint
reftype="1" refid="graphic-25-15-65-950-804-A01">Refer to IPL FIG
4</refint>:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Install the bracket <csn refid="id-4-300"></csn> on the outboard
spreader <csn refid="id-4-30"></csn> with the screw <csn
refid="id-4-365"></csn>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Put the spring <csn refid="id-4-290"></csn> on the bracket <csn
refid="id-4-300"></csn>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Attach with the washers <csn refid="id-4-320"></csn> and <csn
refid="id-4-340"></csn>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Tighten with the screw <csn refid="id-4-330"></csn>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Adjustment</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the lateral front control cables (20) / (30A):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Push on the applicable control pin (100) and make sure that
there is a play.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>If there is no play:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>To adjust tension in the lateral
front control cables (20) or (30A), attach or remove the two nut (220).</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the tilt control cable (50):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Push on the end pusher (130) of the hydrolocks and make sure
that there is a play.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>If there is no play:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>To adjust tension in the tilt
control cable (50), attach or remove the two nut (230).</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>You can also adjust the cable position on the handle (290)
until there is a play.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the longitudinal LH/RH control cables (10).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Push on the applicable locking pin (250) and make sure that
there is a play.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>If there is no play:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist bulltype="ndash"><unlitem><para>To adjust tension in the longitudinal
LH/RH control cables (10), attach or remove the two nut (230).</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Test</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>With the override manual control (330), move the seat upwards
and downwards, and make sure that the cables are not squeezed.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Re-install fairings impacted by installation, <refint
reftype="SUBTASK" refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Cables routing <?Pub _newline></para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the reel locking cable<?Pub _newline><grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-707-a01"></grphcref></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>For the pilot seat: </para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Route the reel locking cable from the inertia reel to the right.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Make the cable go down along the backrest.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cable with a clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Plug the harness cable into the reel locker. </para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>For the copilot seat </para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Route the reel locking cable from the inertia reel to the left.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Make the cable go down along the backrest.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cable with a clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Plug the harness cable into the reel locker. </para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the backrest control cable: <?Pub _newline><grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-707-a01"></grphcref></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Install the tilt control divider on the backrest sheet with
two collars.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Put the two collars in the center of the sheet, the first on
the last row of holes and the second on the third row from the bottom.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Route the control cables to the release handle.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Put on the head of the thigh support cylinder the thigh support
command and safety the cable sheath with the circlips <grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-708-a01"></grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para> Lock the cable on the cylinder with a hose clamp <grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-708-a01"></grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para> Route the control cable between the metal sheet of the pan
seat and the reinforcing tube (See cable with yellow arrow) <grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-708-a01"></grphcref>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the longitudinal locking cables and the rear lateral locking
cable: <?Pub _newline><grphcref refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-709-a01"></grphcref></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Put on the head of the thigh support cylinder the thigh support
command and safety the cable sheath with the circlips.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para> Lock the cables on the cylinder with a hose clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para> Route the control cables between the metal sheet of the pan
seat and the reinforcing tube.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Root the three rear locking cables through the opening of the
cradle crosses to the release handle.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Route the LH pilot seat RH longitudinal control cable and RH
pilot seat LH longitudinal control cable above the spacer (1)</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Route the LH pilot seat LH longitudinal control cable and the
RH pilot seat RH longitudinal control cable below the spacer (1)</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the wire bundle engine cable: <?Pub _newline><grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-710-a01"></grphcref></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Root the wire bundle engine cable from the command bundle button.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Attach at the start the two wires of the control bundle with
a clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Root the cockpit connection part wiring between the seat sheet
and the reinforcement tube "side of the button&rdquo;. Attach with
a clamp before the cradle.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Lock the bundle command on the cable base with a clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>For the second bundle wring, cross the metal sheet of the pan
seat and hold it with a clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Put the cable through the pan seat and the reinforcement tube.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Attach the bundle on the structure before the cradle with a
clamp.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Connect the bundle to the electrical actuator.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For the pneumatic lumbar cable: <?Pub _newline><grphcref
refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-711-a01"></grphcref></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>For the pilot seat: </para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Put the lumbar cable through the space between seat pan sheet
and reinforcement tube.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Put the cable behind the backrest with descending rotation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Pull the cable to the backrest front.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cables to the backrest with a collar.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>For the copilot seat: </para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Put the lumbar cable through the space between seat pan sheet
and reinforcement tube.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Put the cable behind the backrest with descending rotation.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Pull the cable to the backrest front.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cables to the backrest with two collars.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15"
subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="706" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="7001" chg="u" key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-706-A01"
