Bundle Engine Cable </title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-710-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-710-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="711" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-711-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Pneumatic
Lumbar Cable </title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-711-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-711-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-711-A01-02" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-711-A01-02" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-007-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Electrical Actuator</title>
<grphcref refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-712-a01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<title>Put seat on full low position.</title>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Engage lower shaft (545) into lower links (455) and (460).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<title>Engage lower shaft (545) into electrical actuator (500).</title>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Engage upper shaft (505) into spreaders (410). Push shaft manually
and slowly thru lower structure. Engage spacers (510) and safety by
nuts (515).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Connect the electrical connector to electrical actuator (500).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the rod fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="712" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-712-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Actuator</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-712-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-712-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-008-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Restraint System</title>
<grphcref refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-713-a01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put command of restrain system (10) on seat pan structure and
attach with screws (100), washers (110), nuts (120) and sandow.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the two lateral safety belts (10). Attach with shafts
(150), washers (160 and 170) and nuts (180).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the front safety belt (10).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install inertia reel (10) on backrest structure and attach with
screw (20), washers (30) and nut (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the backrest fairing, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the cables routing is correct:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For pilot seat:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Do the routing of the cable to the right side and down along
the backrest tube.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cable to the backrest tube with a collar.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>For copilot seat:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Do the routing of the cable to the left side and down along
the backrest tube.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Attach the cable to the backrest tube with a collar.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15"
subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="713" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="7001" chg="u" key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-713-A01"
revdate="20250131"><title>Installation of Restraint System</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-713-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-713-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Headrest</title>
<grphcref refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-714-a01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Engage the headrest by pulling it downward from the backrest
structure and attach it with the two screws (190).</para>
<?Pub _newline>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="714" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-714-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Headrest</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-714-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-714-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-010-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Fairing</title>
<grphcref refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-715-a01"></grphcref>
<grphcref refid="graphic-25-15-65-991-716-a01"></grphcref>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put bottom inboard fairing (90, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>) and attach
it on seat pan with five screws (100, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put bottom outboard fairing (70, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>) and attach
it on seat pan with four screws (80, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put backrest fairing (10, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>) and attach
it on backrest with four screws (20, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Reinstall headrest assembly, <refint reftype="SUBTASK"
refid="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-009-A01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para> Make sure to route the longitudinal locking cables
as shown <refint reftype="1" refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-716-A01">FIGURE
7016</refint> to prevent any pinching (the cables are below or above
the rear shroud fixation spacers)</para>
</caution>
<para>Put upper link fairing (30, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>) and attach
it on upper link with four screws (40, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put aft fairing (50, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>) and attach
it on backrest with six screws (60, <refint reftype="1"
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01">Fig. 7015</refint>).</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="715" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-715-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Fairing</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-715-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-715-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="716" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-716-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Installation
of Fairing - Longitudinal locking cables</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-716-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-716-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-716-A01-02" sheetnbr="2" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-716-A01-02" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<?Pub _newpage>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="440" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-440-011-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Installation of Upholstery</title>
<refint reftype="1" refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-950-802-A01">(Refer to
IPL FIG. 2)</refint>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Put cushions composed of bottom foam <csn refid="id-2-200"></csn> and
bottom cover <csn refid="id-2-210"></csn>, backrest foam <csn
refid="id-2-230"></csn> and backrest cover <csn refid="id-2-240"></csn> and
the headrest cushion composed of headrest foams <csn refid="id-2-290"></csn>, <csn
refid="id-2-295"></csn>, <csn refid="id-2-300"></csn> and headrest
cover <csn refid="id-2-305"></csn> on their supports.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="8001" chg="u"
key="PGBLK-25-15-65-8001-" revdate="20250131">
<title>FITS AND CLEARANCES</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="940" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8001" chg="u"
key="TASK-25-15-65-940-801-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>General</title>
<topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Torque values</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>No measure of sleeves, bushings, etc. is necessary;
the torque values used are in accordance with usual maintenance practices.
</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>All torque values are standard torque values unless
otherwise specified in assembly block pages and Detailed Parts List.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Maximum permissible (max. after wear)</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>These limits are determined so that re-installed
parts can be used for the period between two overhauls.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>During overhaul which gives the unit a new service life,
and especially for parts ensuring precision guidance of moving components,
the repair facility must endeavor to keep clearances within those
of new parts.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<?Pub _newline>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Type of screw</para>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="801" confltr="A" varnbr="01" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-801-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Type
of Screw</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-801-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-801-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>1.030 m.daN (91.16 lbf.in) for screw in tensile
stress.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>0.900 m.daN (79.66 lbf.in) for screw in shearing stress.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Torque is the measurement of the turning or twisting
force applied to an object. This chart shows the recommended minimum
and maximum torque values applicable for each Safran Seats (Safran
seats France) screw types on non-lubricated metal parts.</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>Torque values are in N.m (multiply by 8.8507 to obtain
lbf.in).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Recommendations related to the quantities consumed annually:</para><?Pub
_newline>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="802" confltr="a" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-802-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Annual
Quantity Recommendations</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-802-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-802-A01-01" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-802-A01-02" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-802-A01-02" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-802-A01-03" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-802-A01-03" revdate="20250131"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
