</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Job set-up</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Make sure that the equipment is free of damage.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Install the protective materials on the equipment with their
blanking plugs.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic><?Pub Dtl><title>Procedure</title>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="550" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-550-001-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Preservation</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>USE A SOFT CLOTH MOISTENED WITH ALIPHATIC NAPHTHA,
GRADE F TO CLEAN THE EXTERNAL PARTS OF THE SEAT.</para>
</caution>
<para>Set the armrests to the down position.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Tilt the backrest forward.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Lightly grease the hinge points with grease "182 DS" or equivalent.
</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="550" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="15001" chg="u"
key="SUBTASK-25-15-65-550-002-A01" revdate="20250131">
<title>Storage</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>DO NOT LIFT AND MOVE THE SEATS BY THE ARMRESTS.</para>
</caution>
<para>For long storage, wrap equipment assembly in waterproof wrapping
paper or a plastic cover.</para>
<note><para>For painted parts, we recommend a black or dark protection.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Identify equipment part number and date of overhaul on a tag
or in a convenient location on the equipment wrapper.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Place the equipment on a soft plane material. The equipment
must rest on clean, non abrasive and non corrosive surfaces.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Store equipment in cool, dry place away from sunlight and heat
sources with a good supply of air.</para>
<note><para>Keep the relative humidity at between 45% and 55% with
a temperature range from 18.0&deg;C to 25.0&deg;C (64.4&deg;F to 77.0&deg;F).
</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>No loads should be placed on the stored equipment, in particular
the equipment should not be stacked.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Equipment has to be tested before installation, examine all
the equipment systems, <refint reftype="1" refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-5001-">(refer
to Page Block 5001) "CHECK"</refint> and <refint reftype="1"
refid="PGBLK-25-15-65-1001-">(refer to Page Block 1001) "TESTING AND
FAULT ISOLATION"</refint> of this manual.</para>
<note><para>If the equipment is fitted with hydrolocks, a handling
is required every 3 months (Compression cycle).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15"
subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="1501" confltr="A" varnbr="01"
pgblknbr="15001" chg="u" key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1501-A01"
revdate="20250131"><title>Storage</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1501-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1501-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic></task>
</pgblk>
<ipl chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" pgblknbr="10001" confnbr="1"
chg="u" key="IPL-25-15-65-10000-1" revdate="20250131">
<title>ILLUSTRATED PARTS LIST</title>
<iplintro>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="99F" seq="801"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001" chg="u"
key="Task-25-15-65-99F-801-A01" revdate="20250131"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Introduction</title>
<topic>
<title>General</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The Illustrated Part List (IPL) contains the illustrations and
the parts lists of the component(s) shown on the title page. The parts
lists give the items which can be disassembled, repaired or replaced,
and assembled.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic></task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="99F" seq="802"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001" chg="u"
key="Task-25-15-65-99F-802-A01" revdate="20250131"><?Pub Dtl>
<title>Explanation and Usage of Section</title>
<topic>
<title>Assembly Order Indenture System</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The indenture system used in the parts list shows the relation
of the parts to each other. For a given item, the number of indentures
shows the relation of the item to the next higher assembly as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>1 2 3</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Assembly</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>&#8901; Detail parts for Assembly</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>&#8901; Attaching Parts for Assembly</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>&#8901;&#8901; Subassembly</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>&#8901;&#8901; Attaching parts for Subassembly</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>&#8901;&#8901;&#8901; Detail parts for Subassembly</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Effectivity Code</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>In IPL figures that have more than one top assembly item, reference
letters (A, B, C, etc.) are given to each top assembly item in the
EFFECT CODE column. The reference letter of the applicable top assembly
is also shown in the EFFECT CODE column for each detail part and subassembly,
except that no reference letter is shown for detail parts and subassemblies
used on all top assemblies.</para>
<note><para>The effectivity code identifies affected parts within
a single figure only. The same code can appear in other figures, but
it is only to be used for those parts within the figure in which it
is listed. Effectivity does not necessarily relate to more than one
figure.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Units Per Assembly</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The UNITS PER ASSY column shows the total number of units required
per assembly, per subassembly, and per sub-subassembly as applicable.
For bulk items, the abbreviation AR is used for "as required". The
abbreviation RF shows the item is listed for reference purposes.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The abbreviation &ldquo;NP&rdquo; besides the quantity shows
the item is &rdquo;NOT PROCURABLE&rdquo;. The abbreviation &ldquo;RPD&rdquo;
besides the quantity shows the item is &rdquo;REPLACED&rdquo;. The
abbreviation &ldquo;SPD&rdquo; besides the quantity shows the item
is &rdquo;SUPERSEDED&rdquo;, the abbreviation &ldquo;BFE&rdquo; besides
the quantity shows the item is &ldquo;BFE&rdquo;.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Parts Replacement Data</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>The interchangeability relationship between parts is identified
in the NOMENCLATURE column of the parts list. A list of the terms
used to show interchangeability and their definition is as follows:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="11" subjnbr="58" func="997" seq="10001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001"
id="Table-25-15-65-997-10001-A01">
<tgroup cols="3"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="0.75*"><colspec
colname="col2" colwidth="0.56*"><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="1.70*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry namest="col1" nameend="col3" valign="middle" align="center">
<para>Interchangeability Definitions</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Term</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Parts List Abbreviation</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Definition</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>Alternative part</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>ALT P/N</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>This part is alternative to and interchangeable with other parts in the same item number variant group or other item number if designated
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>Superseded by</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>SUPSD BY</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>The part in the part number column is replaced by and is not interchangeable with the item number shown in the notation
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>Supersedes</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>SUPSDS</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>The part in the part number column replaces and is not interchangeable with the item number shown in the notation
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>Replaced by</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>RPLD BY</para>
</entry>
<entry rowsep="0">
<para>The part in the part number column is replaced by and interchangeable with the item number shown in the notation
</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Replaces</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>RPLS</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>The part in the part number column replaces and is interchangeable with the item number shown in the notation
</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Items Not Illustrated</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Items not illustrated are shown by a dash (-) in front of the
item number in the FIG. and ITEM NO. column.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Alpha Variant Item Numbers</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Alpha variants A-Z (except I and O) are added to existing item
numbers when necessary to show:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Added items</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Service Bulletin modifications</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Configuration differences</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Optional parts</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Product improvement parts (non service bulletin).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Alpha variant item numbers are not shown in the illustration
when the appearance and location of the alpha variant item is the
same as the basic item.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Locating Parts</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>To find a part with a known Part Number (P/N).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Refer to the Numerical Index and find the P/N.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Read across to the related figure and item numbers.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Refer to the figure in the parts list.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Find the item number on the illustration.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>To find a subassembly P/N from a known assembly P/N.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Refer to the Numerical Index and find the assembly P/N.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Read across to find the related figure and item numbers.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Refer to the related IPL figure and find the item number of
the known assembly. This will give an indented breakdown of the assembly
P/N.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Cross reference with the related illustration and IPL for the
subassembly item number.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<title>Part numbers codification</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Standard Part Numbers</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Standard international standard part numbers
is mentioned in Part Number column : i.e. NAS601-5.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Internal Safran Seats France&rsquo;s standard parts
numbers codification is mentioned in Nomenclature Column: (VINAS6015)
like vendor code.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, VINAS6015 = NAS601-5</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples: VIAN412A = AN4-12A, R0AN960416 = AN960-416</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples: R0AN960416 = AN960-416</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples: EEP79312-M03 = P79312-M03</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples: VE-192821250N = 192821-250N</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples: CI7133D5 = 7133D5</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples: NAS60x-x = NAS60x-xP, NAS1149Dxxxx = NAS1149DxxxxK
</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>For Safran Seats France code and Description, refer
to the <refint reftype="TABLE" refid="Table-25-15-65-997-10002-A01">Table-25-15-65-997-10002-A01
</refint></para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Safran Seats (Safran seats France) code</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
