<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Safran Seats France&rsquo;s Parts Number</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Standard Safran Seats France&rsquo;s Parts number codification
is:</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>2 digits - 6 digits - 3 digits - 1 digit.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Thus, XX &ndash; xxxXXX &ndash; xxx &ndash; X.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Example: 50-000400-100-0 or 65-000600-800-0</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Occasionally a &laquo;A&raquo; can appear between the 8th and
9th digit.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, XX &ndash; xxxXXX A xxx &ndash; X</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Example: 65-000600A800-0 = 65-000600-800-0</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Occasionally a &laquo;R&raquo; can appear between the 11th and
12th digit.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, XX &ndash; xxxXXX - xxx R X</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>65-000600-800-0 = 65-000600-800R0</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>65-000600A800-0 = 65-000600A800R0 (a and b)</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Occasionally a triple &laquo;000&raquo; can be missed between
the 2nd and 6th digit.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, XX &ndash; XXX &ndash; xxx &ndash; X</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>65-600-800-0 = 65-000600-800-0</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>65-000600-800-0 = 65-600A800R0 (a, b and c)</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Occasionally a &laquo;1&raquo; can appear instead of the first
dash &laquo;-&raquo;.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, XX 1 xxxXXX &ndash; xxx &ndash; X</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>65-000600-800-0 = 651000600-800-0</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>65-000600-800-0 = 651600A800R0 (a, b, c, and d)</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>In order to include the color code information in the part number,
the dashes have been removed and color code added at the end of the
P/N.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, XX &ndash; xxxXXX &ndash; xxx &ndash;
X with color code Hxxx became XXxxxXXXxxxXxxx</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>65-000600-800-0 with color code H108 became
650006008000108</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>651600A800R0 with color code H108 became 650006008000108
(a, b, c ,d and e)</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>G081309-517 with color code AK became G081309AK517</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>New Safran Seats France&rsquo;s Parts number codification is
only: "F0" and 6 digits.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, F0xxxxxx.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>F0414381</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>F0450563</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Safran Seats France Article Code Reference</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Under each part, we indicate a Safran Seats
France article code (REF: xxxxxx) as additional information in the
"1234567 nomenclature" column of the CMM.</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Thus, 65-000240-100-1 = 063374</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>650006008000108 = 047323P108</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>P79312-M03 = 272507</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="10001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1001" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-15-65-991-1001-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Safran
Seats France Article Code Reference</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1001-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1001-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Integration of the letter 'F' in front of the article code.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Further to the ERP change, the article code
codification (REF: xxxxxx) became (REF: Fxxxxxx):</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Thus, 16-100200-011-0 = F324566</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>650006008000108 = F047323P108</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>P79312-M03 = F272507</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>P79387A070 = F0414381</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus : (REF: xxxxxx) = (REF: Fxxxxxx)</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Examples:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>047323P108 = F047323P108</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>272507 = F272507</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="1002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-15-65-991-1002-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Integration
of the Letter 'F' in Front of the Article Code</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1002-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1002-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>The supplier P/N could be also given as information when the
part number indicated on the column part number is a F0xxxxxx type.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Thus, F0414381 = P79387A070</para>
</unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Example: F0414380 = P33711M060</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="1003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1003-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Supplier
P/N</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1003-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1003-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>Addition Of Color Code Into Part Number</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Integration of color code into part number</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>To include the color information into the part
number, the dashes have been removed and color code added at the end
of the part number.</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>Example: P/N 50-000610-024-0 with color code H022 Becomes
500006100240022</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>These part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>The new codification has been introduced in
all CMM initial release or revision issued after June 10th 2005 (see
example <grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1004-A01"></grphcref>).</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<para>Addition of Supplier Number (REF) in the CMM</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Each Safran Seats France part has a Supplier
Number indicated on its identification label <grphcref
refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1005-A01"></grphcref>. This REF number
has been added as additional information in the "1234567 nomenclature"
column of the CMM <grphcref refid="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1004-A01"></grphcref>.
</para></unlitem>
<unlitem><para>It is recommended to the customer to add this Supplier
Number (REF) in the purchase order to improve delay and reliability
in spare part data processing.</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991" seq="1004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1004-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Example
of CMM modification</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1004-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1004-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="1005" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10001" chg="u"
key="GRAPHIC-25-15-65-991-1005-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Identification
Label</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1005-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1005-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic><topic>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<para>Screws codification</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>Safran Seats (Safran seats France) reference
with correspondence P/N normalized of screw reference:</para></unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>Old and new screw part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
</prcitem><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="15" subjnbr="65" func="991"
seq="1006" confltr="A" varnbr="01" confnbr="01" chg="u"
key="Graphic-25-15-65-991-1006-A01" revdate="20250131"><title>Screws
Codification</title>
<sheet gnbr="graphic25-15-65-991-1006-A01-01" sheetnbr="1" imgarea="bp"
chg="u" key="graphic25-15-65-991-1006-A01-01" revdate="20250131">
</sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<para>New screws codification information</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<unlist><unlitem><para>To limit to 15 digits the screw part number
and to prevent screw corrosion with a new treatment (black screws
become grey), Safran Seats (Safran seats France) change the screw
codification as shown on the chart below:</para>
</unlitem>
</unlist>
<note><para>Old and new screw part numbers are two ways interchangeable.</para>
</note>
<note><para>All screws P/N NAS60x-x are replaced by P/N NAS60x-xP.</para>
</note>
<note><para>All screws P/N NAS60xx are replaced by P/N NAS60xxP.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
